data: {"channels": ["bm25", "dense"], "bm25_count": 120, "dense_count": 120, "hits": [{"chunk_id": "c_210df222c632", "paper_id": "p_093639f6b110", "section_path": "Acknowledgements", "score": 0.3704, "rrf": 0.064004, "kind": "detail", "aspect": "各论文提出的核心方法与技术路径", "rerank": null, "text": "orav, Ma-\nsoud Mokhtari, Xavier Gabaix, Marco Garosi, Vincent Schönbach, Avishek Mondal, Victor\nS.C.\nLui, Sumit Bhatia, Julian Asilis, Hengchao Chen, Siavash Khallaghi, Csaba Szepesvári,\nMike Singer, Mykhailo Shvets, Abdalla Ibrahim, Stefan Hell, Ron Raphaeli, Diogo Tavares,\nAristotelis Siozopoulos,", "page": 11}, {"chunk_id": "c_c0c08a674bb2", "paper_id": "p_5e84333e8e1d", "section_path": "_front", "score": 5.0376, "rrf": 0.063101, "kind": "detail", "aspect": "各论文提出的核心方法与技术路径", "rerank": null, "text": "Provided proper attribution is provided, Google hereby grants permission to\nreproduce the tables and figures in this paper solely for use in journalistic or\nscholarly works.\nAttention Is All You Need\nAshish Vaswani∗\nNoam Shazeer∗\nGoogle Brain\navaswani@google.com\nGoogle Brain\nnoam@google.com\nLlion Jo", "page": 1}, {"chunk_id": "c_5168490af823", "paper_id": "p_5e84333e8e1d", "section_path": "_front", "score": 0.3505, "rrf": 0.061538, "kind": "detail", "aspect": "各论文提出的核心方法与技术路径", "rerank": null, "text": "Kaiser∗\nGoogle Brain\nlukaszkaiser@google.com\nIllia Polosukhin∗‡\nillia.polosukhin@gmail.com\nAbstract\nThe dominant sequence transduction models are based on complex recurrent or\nconvolutional neural networks that include an encoder and a decoder. The best\nperforming models also connect the encoder and", "page": 1}, {"chunk_id": "c_90b781e6e1d4", "paper_id": "p_093639f6b110", "section_path": "Acknowledgements", "score": 0.3592, "rrf": 0.061327, "kind": "detail", "aspect": "各论文提出的核心方法与技术路径", "rerank": null, "text": "l Sheikh, Ja-\ncob Horton, Felix Rammell, Sasha Luccioni, Akshil Patel, Alessandro Gentilini, Kevin M\nercier,\nKrzysztof Lichocki, Chuck Krapf, Brian Ha, Chris Kang, Leonardo Viotti, Kai Li, Himan Ab-\ndollahpouri, Ari Pakman, Giuseppe Antonio Di Luna, Dan Oneat,ă, Conrad Whiteley, Joseph\nSantarcangelo", "page": 11}, {"chunk_id": "c_a89116a3c66c", "paper_id": "p_a19a95dbf468", "section_path": "_front", "score": 0.3389, "rrf": 0.061004, "kind": "detail", "aspect": "各论文提出的核心方法与技术路径", "rerank": null, "text": "Ashish Vaswani∗\nGoogle Brain\navaswani@google.com\nNoam Shazeer∗\nGoogle Brain\nnoam@google.com\nNiki Parmar∗\nGoogle Research\nnikip@google.com\nJakob Uszkoreit∗\nGoogle Research\nusz@google.com\nLlion Jones∗\nGoogle Research\nllion@google.com\nAidan N. Gomez∗ †\nUniversity of Toronto\naidan@cs.toronto.edu\nŁukasz ", "page": 1}, {"chunk_id": "c_6b294a42c474", "paper_id": "p_093639f6b110", "section_path": "_front", "score": 0.3001, "rrf": 0.058869, "kind": "detail", "aspect": "各论文提出的核心方法与技术路径", "rerank": null, "text": "Understanding Deep Learning\nSimon J.D. Prince\nFebruary 8, 2026\nThe most recent version of this document can be found at http://udlbook.com.\nCopyright in this work has been licensed exclusively to The MIT Press,\nhttps://mitpress.mit.edu, which released the final version to the public in December 2023", "page": 1}, {"chunk_id": "c_160c22f5d504", "paper_id": "p_5e84333e8e1d", "section_path": "Embeddings and Softmax", "score": 6.5764, "rrf": 0.047228, "kind": "detail", "aspect": "各论文提出的核心方法与技术路径", "rerank": null, "text": "ation that can\nbe parallelized, as measured by the minimum number of sequential operations required.\nThe third is the path length between long-range dependencies in the network. Learning long-range\ndependencies is a key challenge in many sequence transduction tasks. One key factor affecting the\nabil", "page": 6}, {"chunk_id": "c_5b09b1387b62", "paper_id": "p_a19a95dbf468", "section_path": "4 Why Self-Attention", "score": 6.5764, "rrf": 0.046724, "kind": "detail", "aspect": "各论文提出的核心方法与技术路径", "rerank": null, "text": "ation that can\nbe parallelized, as measured by the minimum number of sequential operations required.\nThe third is the path length between long-range dependencies in the network. Learning long-range\ndependencies is a key challenge in many sequence transduction tasks. One key factor affecting the\nabil", "page": 5}]}

