data: {"channels": ["bm25", "dense"], "bm25_count": 0, "dense_count": 192, "hits": [{"chunk_id": "c_c67976e582f8", "paper_id": "p_a19a95dbf468", "section_path": "_front", "score": 0.3728, "rrf": 0.065574, "kind": "detail", "aspect": "各论文提出的核心方法与技术路径", "rerank": null, "text": "edu\nŁukasz Kaiser∗\nGoogle Brain\nlukaszkaiser@google.com\nIllia Polosukhin∗\nillia.polosukhin@gmail.com\nThe dominant sequence transduction models are based on complex recurrent or\nconvolutional neural networks in an encoder-decoder configuration. The best\nperforming models also connect the encoder and ", "page": 1}, {"chunk_id": "c_5168490af823", "paper_id": "p_5e84333e8e1d", "section_path": "_front", "score": 0.3936, "rrf": 0.065574, "kind": "detail", "aspect": "各论文提出的核心方法与技术路径", "rerank": null, "text": "Kaiser∗\nGoogle Brain\nlukaszkaiser@google.com\nIllia Polosukhin∗‡\nillia.polosukhin@gmail.com\nAbstract\nThe dominant sequence transduction models are based on complex recurrent or\nconvolutional neural networks that include an encoder and a decoder. The best\nperforming models also connect the encoder and", "page": 1}, {"chunk_id": "c_6b294a42c474", "paper_id": "p_093639f6b110", "section_path": "_front", "score": 0.3293, "rrf": 0.064332, "kind": "detail", "aspect": "各论文提出的核心方法与技术路径", "rerank": null, "text": "Understanding Deep Learning\nSimon J.D. Prince\nFebruary 8, 2026\nThe most recent version of this document can be found at http://udlbook.com.\nCopyright in this work has been licensed exclusively to The MIT Press,\nhttps://mitpress.mit.edu, which released the final version to the public in December 2023", "page": 1}, {"chunk_id": "c_c0c08a674bb2", "paper_id": "p_5e84333e8e1d", "section_path": "_front", "score": 0.3879, "rrf": 0.064012, "kind": "detail", "aspect": "各论文提出的核心方法与技术路径", "rerank": null, "text": "Provided proper attribution is provided, Google hereby grants permission to\nreproduce the tables and figures in this paper solely for use in journalistic or\nscholarly works.\nAttention Is All You Need\nAshish Vaswani∗\nNoam Shazeer∗\nGoogle Brain\navaswani@google.com\nGoogle Brain\nnoam@google.com\nLlion Jo", "page": 1}, {"chunk_id": "c_eb3ac15b64de", "paper_id": "p_a19a95dbf468", "section_path": "7 Conclusion", "score": 0.3652, "rrf": 0.064004, "kind": "detail", "aspect": "各论文提出的核心方法与技术路径", "rerank": null, "text": "In this work, we presented the Transformer, the first sequence transduction model based entirely on\nattention, replacing the recurrent layers most commonly used in encoder-decoder architectures with\nmulti-headed self-attention.\nFor translation tasks, the Transformer can be trained significantly fast", "page": 10}, {"chunk_id": "c_7dccadb30c62", "paper_id": "p_a19a95dbf468", "section_path": "1 Introduction", "score": 0.3379, "rrf": 0.0635, "kind": "summary", "aspect": "各论文提出的核心方法与技术路径", "rerank": null, "text": "[章节概览] 1 Introduction（pp.0-0）：Recurrent neural networks, long short-term memory [12] and gated recurrent [7] neural networks\nin particular, have been firmly established as state of the art approaches in sequence modeling and\ntransduction problems such as language modeling and machine translation [31", "page": 1}, {"chunk_id": "c_210df222c632", "paper_id": "p_093639f6b110", "section_path": "Acknowledgements", "score": 0.4115, "rrf": 0.063321, "kind": "detail", "aspect": "各论文提出的核心方法与技术路径", "rerank": null, "text": "orav, Ma-\nsoud Mokhtari, Xavier Gabaix, Marco Garosi, Vincent Schönbach, Avishek Mondal, Victor\nS.C.\nLui, Sumit Bhatia, Julian Asilis, Hengchao Chen, Siavash Khallaghi, Csaba Szepesvári,\nMike Singer, Mykhailo Shvets, Abdalla Ibrahim, Stefan Hell, Ron Raphaeli, Diogo Tavares,\nAristotelis Siozopoulos,", "page": 11}, {"chunk_id": "c_90b781e6e1d4", "paper_id": "p_093639f6b110", "section_path": "Acknowledgements", "score": 0.4098, "rrf": 0.063056, "kind": "detail", "aspect": "各论文提出的核心方法与技术路径", "rerank": null, "text": "l Sheikh, Ja-\ncob Horton, Felix Rammell, Sasha Luccioni, Akshil Patel, Alessandro Gentilini, Kevin M\nercier,\nKrzysztof Lichocki, Chuck Krapf, Brian Ha, Chris Kang, Leonardo Viotti, Kai Li, Himan Ab-\ndollahpouri, Ari Pakman, Giuseppe Antonio Di Luna, Dan Oneat,ă, Conrad Whiteley, Joseph\nSantarcangelo", "page": 11}]}

